            <ArticleTitle>Intracranial solitary fibrous tumor/hemangiopericytoma: Report of two cases and literature review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intracranial solitary fibrous tumors (ISFTs) are rare mesenchymal neoplasms originating in the meninges and constitute a heterogeneous group of rare spindle cell tumors that include benign and malignant neoplasms of which hemangiopericytoma is nowadays considered a cellular phenotypic variant. ISFT usually shows benign or indolent clinical behavior. We describe two cases of ISFT managed in our institution along with a review of pertinent literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
